            <ArticleTitle>Disclosing a diagnosis of acute coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>212-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The disclosure of bad news is one of the most difficult tasks of a physician. This study explores how physicians prefer to disclose bad news to patients with acute coronary disease in emergency centres in Iran, and to their families.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
